          "title": "You'll want to know: ઓરડો",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઓરડો — orḍo — \"room\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "આ મારો ઓરડો છે. — ā māro orḍo che — \"This is my room.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઓરડો (orḍo) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from apavaraka, \"inner apartment\", and CDIAL glosses the Gujarati word \"principal room\" (CDIAL 450)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
